-- title:
--   Existence of a resolved model with étale crossing charts
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $N_0\ge 1$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a level-$N_0q$ Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN` on the Igusa scheme $X(N_0,q)$ over $R=R(q)$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O\colon R(q)\to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $q$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with $O\to\kappa$. Write $\mathfrak X_O$ for the fibre product of $X(N_0,q)\to\operatorname{Spec}R(q)$ with $\operatorname{Spec}O$, and call crossings the points of the fibre product of the two maps $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ 0$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ 1$ (the intersection of the two copies of the level-$N_0$ fibre in the geometric fibre). Two hypotheses are assumed. First, rationality: every crossing, pushed into $\mathfrak X_O$ by `DRLevel.bcMap`, is the image of the closed point under some section of the fibre of $X(N_0,q)$ over the residue field of $O$. Second, oriented étale-type charts: each crossing $n$ admits an $e\ge 1$, an open $U$ of $\mathfrak X_O$ containing the image $x_n$ of $n$, and a morphism $f\colon U\to\operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-q^{e})\bigr)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}O$ such that, for $y\in U$, both coordinates $U(q^e),V(q^e)$ lie in the prime $f(y)$ exactly when $y=x_n$; at $y=x_n$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal and induces an isomorphism of residue fields; and $V(q^e)\in f(y)$ holds precisely when $y$ lies in the image of the $0$-branch $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\ \kappa\ 0$, and $U(q^e)\in f(y)$ precisely when $y$ lies in the image of the $1$-branch. The conclusion asserts the existence of a resolved model package $\mathcal Y$ of type `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel N₀ q 𝔛 O ρO κ toκ` (an integral, locally Noetherian scheme $Y$, proper and flat over $\operatorname{Spec}O$ and proper over $\mathfrak X_O$, with regular stalks of Krull dimension at most $2$ away from the locus where $q$ is invertible, isomorphic to $\mathfrak X_O$ over the preimage of the smooth locus and over the generic fibre, with a finite type of nodes of widths $\ge 1$ in bijection with the crossings and invertible integral ideal sheaves indexed by the subdivided dual graph whose product is the ideal generated by $q$, together with the remaining data of that structure), and of a family $F_c$ of ideal sheaf data $F_c\,e\,k$ on the chain resolution $\mathrm{Resolution}\ q\ e$ for $e\in\mathbb N$ and $k\in\{0,\dots,e\}$, such that: the restriction of $F_c\,e\,k$ along the $i$-th chart inclusion $\mathrm{Resolution.\iota}\ q\ e\ i$ is the ideal sheaf on $\operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-q)\bigr)$ cut out by $V(q)$ if $k=i$, by $U(q)$ if $k=i+1$, and by the unit ideal otherwise; and the type of `DRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam` data for $F_c$ on the ramified repackaging `DRResolvedModelPackageLevelRam.ofUnramified 𝒴` (uniformiser the image of $q$) is nonempty, i.e. $\mathcal Y$ carries étale crossing charts over $\operatorname{Spec}O$ around each node, identified after base change along the resolution with $Y$ over those charts and labelling the components in accordance with $F_c$.
--
--   This is the existence statement for the minimal regular model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over a discrete valuation ring with residue characteristic $q$, in the form of a resolved Deligne–Rapoport package together with étale charts on the crossings: the two copies of $X_0(N_0)$ in the special fibre are joined at the supersingular points by chains of exceptional rational curves, the chain over a crossing of thickness $e$ having $e-1$ members. The oriented étale crossing charts are taken as hypotheses here, so this is a producer that converts local chart data into the global resolved model; it is used in the variant that additionally records the bijection of nodes with supersingular places and the compatibility of the chart exponents with the arithmetic widths.
